   304	def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
   305	    """
   306	    Assemble scattered sprites into a single relay chain whose color groups must alternate.
   307	
   308	    Input structure:
   309	    - bg = black (0). One yellow anchor sprite stays fixed while several colored sprites are scattered apart.
   310	    - Cool-colored sprites (blue / azure) are main sprites; warm-colored sprites (pink / orange) are auxiliary sprites.
   311	    - Every connector is a 2-cell red (2) boundary port, and the anchor exposes exactly one such port.
   312	
   313	    Rule:
   314	    - Start from the anchor's red port and grow exactly one chain.
   315	    - The first attached sprite must be a main sprite; after that, each next sprite must attach only to the current chain tail and must switch role relative to the previous sprite.
   316	    - Keep relaying the tail forward until all sprites are consumed and the last sprite closes the chain with no unused port left.
   317	
   318	    Key insight:
